    <string name="ask_welcome">Hi! I\'m Verde. Ask me where anything goes, or send me a scan.</string>
    <string name="answer_class_format">%1$s → %2$s. %3$s</string>
    <string name="answer_batteries">Never put batteries in a bin, they can start fires. Take them to a battery drop-off point; most supermarkets have one.</string>
    <string name="answer_pizza">Only the clean parts. Tear off the greasy bits for food or general waste, then recycle the clean lid.</string>
    <string name="answer_coffee_cup">Most takeaway cups have a plastic lining, so they need a cup recycling point, not your home bin. The plastic lid can usually go in recycling.</string>
    <string name="answer_crisps">Not in most household recycling. Many supermarkets have soft-plastic drop-off points instead.</string>
    <string name="answer_electronics">Electronics and cables shouldn\'t go in any bin. Take them to a household recycling centre or an electrical drop-off point.</string>
    <string name="answer_hello">Hello! Ask me about any item, or tap the camera to scan it.</string>
    <string name="answer_unknown">I\'m not sure about that one. Scan it and I\'ll tell you which bin it belongs in.</string>

